# Customer Sales & Analytics

## Overview

This project focuses on analyzing customer sales data to understand revenue performance, purchasing behavior, seasonal trends, and key business performance drivers.

The analysis transforms sales data into actionable business insights related to revenue, purchases, discounts, customer behavior, and category performance.

## Objectives

- Analyze overall sales and revenue performance
- Understand customer purchasing behavior
- Identify revenue trends
- Analyze sales performance across categories
- Evaluate the impact of discounts
- Identify seasonal sales patterns
- Identify key factors influencing business performance
- Develop data-driven recommendations

## Key Performance Metrics

| Metric | Value |
|---|---:|
| Total Revenue | $165K |
| Total Purchases | 3,960 |
| Average Rating | 3.77 |
| Total Discounts | $29K |

## Analysis Areas

### 1. Revenue Analysis

The project analyzes revenue trends to understand business performance over time and identify important changes in sales.

### 2. Category Performance

Sales performance is analyzed across different product categories to understand their contribution to overall business performance.

### 3. Customer Behavior

The analysis examines customer purchasing behavior and identifies important purchasing patterns and customer-related performance indicators.

### 4. Seasonal Sales Analysis

Seasonal trends are analyzed to identify periods of stronger and weaker sales performance.

### 5. Discount Analysis

The project examines discounts and their relationship with sales performance to support better revenue optimization and discount decisions.

## Key Business Insights

The analysis focuses on:

- Revenue performance
- Customer purchasing patterns
- Category-level sales performance
- Seasonal sales trends
- Discount effectiveness
- Customer acquisition
- Revenue optimization

